# arc6 pruning fix — the SigRel split, MEASURED AND NOT SHIPPED.
#
# The honest implementation of A6-FX3's registered remedy: separate the
# PRUNING relation (coarse: list == tuple) from the SEMANTIC relation
# (exact), with the spec-target check moved BEFORE the equivalence lookup
# so the coarser relation can never hide a candidate that satisfies the
# spec, and `exclude` refutations kept on their own exact relation.
#
# NOT SHIPPED because the premise it addresses is refuted: case 1 was never
# a pruning explosion (see PROGRAM_SYNTHESIS_ARC6_PRUNING_FIX.md 1.3).
# Measured cost/benefit: distinct 16,148 -> 15,980 (-1.0%) on searches that
# are unsatisfiable by construction; ZERO change on every search that solves.
# Apply with: patch -p0 runners/dsl/src/synth_enumerate.rs < this file
#
